# Three deploy targets share this codebase — keep values scoped to the
# right one, not copy-pasted across:
#   1. Local dev      — frontend (:3000) + Studio (:3333) both run together.
#   2. Vercel ("test") — e.g. test.getresume.dev. The editing-capable tier:
#      full Next.js server, draft mode, Presentation Tool, SanityLive. Set
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_STEGA_ENABLED=true and NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_STUDIO_URL
#      here, in Vercel's dashboard — never in a local .env file.
#   3. Cloudflare Pages ("production") — e.g. jatin.getresume.dev. A static
#      export via `npm run build:cf-static`, everything editing-related
#      stripped for performance. NEXT_PUBLIC_DEPLOY_TARGET=cloudflare forces
#      stega off here regardless of any other setting (see sanity/lib/api.ts).
# A value that's right for one tier (e.g. the Studio's production URL) is
# actively wrong in another (breaks local dev) — this is exactly the bug
# that prompted this comment.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID="<paste your project here>" # Required - The ID of your Sanity project
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET="production" # Required - The dataset of your Sanity project
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION="2025-09-25" # Optional - The API version provided to the Sanity Client
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_STUDIO_URL="" #Optional, defaults to http://localhost:3333
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_STEGA_ENABLED="" #Optional, "true"/"false". Defaults to true outside production, false in production. Set to "true" on Vercel's production env so the Presentation Tool's live preview gets click-to-edit. Ignored on the Cloudflare static build (NEXT_PUBLIC_DEPLOY_TARGET=cloudflare, set inline by npm run build:cf-static) — always off there regardless of this value.
SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN="<paste your token here>" # Required - The read token for your Sanity project
SITE_AUTHOR_SLUG="" # Required - slug of the person document that is the site's canonical author (must match SANITY_STUDIO_SITE_AUTHOR_SLUG in studio/.env)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://jatin.getresume.dev" #Optional - canonical site URL used for SEO metadata/og:url. Defaults to https://jatin.getresume.dev
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID="" #Optional - Google Analytics measurement ID. Leave unset to disable analytics.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEPLOY_TARGET="" #Optional - set to "cloudflare" only by `npm run build:cf-static`. Leave unset for the normal Vercel/Node build.

# Translate feature (Studio's "Auto-translate" field action) — all optional,
# leave unset to disable the feature entirely.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL="http://localhost:11434" #Optional - defaults to http://127.0.0.1:11434
OLLAMA_DEFAULT_MODEL="" #Optional - defaults to "translategemma"
TRANSLATE_TIMEOUT_MS="" #Optional - defaults to 30000
# Origins allowed to call /api/translate cross-origin (comma-separated), e.g.
# the Studio's own URL. Leave unset to allow same-origin requests only. This
# is the endpoint's real access control — see app/api/translate/route.ts for
# why there's no shared-secret auth here (the caller is a static Studio SPA
# with no server, so nothing it sends can stay secret).
TRANSLATE_CORS_ORIGINS=""
RESUME_CACHE_TTL_MS="" #Optional - in-memory resume data cache TTL in ms, defaults to 60000
